# GitHub OAuth App configuration. Copy this file to `.env.local` (or `.env`)
# and fill in real values from your own GitHub OAuth App
# (https://github.com/settings/developers).
#
# The redirect URI is computed automatically at runtime from wherever the
# app is served (see `shared/config/oauth.ts`) — it is NOT configured here.
# Whatever origin(s) you run the app from must be registered as a Redirect
# URI on the OAuth App itself, e.g. `http://localhost:5173/oauth/callback`
# for `npm run dev`, and additionally `http://localhost:4173/oauth/callback`
# if you also test `npm run preview`.
#
# NOTE: per this assignment's requirements, the client secret is used
# directly from the browser (kept in localStorage alongside the access
# token). A real production app must exchange the OAuth code for a token via
# a backend/BFF instead of shipping the client secret to the browser.

VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
